===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

[[File:06 Restoration of gilded mirror in Muzeum Gornoslaskie, Bytom, Poland - furniture restorer working.jpg|thumb|right|The '''restoration''' of antique mirror involved repainting its frame.]]

# The process of bringing an object back to its [[original]] [[state]]; the process of [[restore|restoring]] something.
#* '''1921''', {{w|T.S. Eliot}}, ''The Sacred Wood'', "The Possibility of a Poetic Drama":
#*: There is all the difference between preservation and '''restoration'''.
#: {{ux|en|[[foreskin]] '''restoration'''}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''restoration''' of this painting will take years.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''restoration''' of this medieval church involved undoing all the Victorian modifications.}}
# The [[return]] of a [[former]] [[monarchy]] or [[monarch]] to [[power]], usually after having been forced to step down.
#* '''1680''', {{w|John Dryden}}, ''Albion and Albanius'', Act I, secene 1:
#*: Behold the differing climes agree
#*: Rejoicing in thy '''restoration'''.
#: {{ux|en|The '''restoration''' of the House of Stuart took place a few years after the death of Cromwell.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''restoration''' of the Kingdom of Spain took place immediately after the death of Franco.}}
# {{lb|en|theology}} The [[receive|receiving]] of a [[sinner]] to [[divine]] [[favor]].

